@base = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@tenant1 = tenant1.localhost
@tenant2 = tenant2.localhost

### 1. Who am I? (tenant1)
GET {{base}}/api/me
Host: {{tenant1}}

### 1. Who am I? (tenant2)
GET {{base}}/api/me
Host: {{tenant2}}

### 2. tenant1 sees only its own expenses
# @name tenant1List
GET {{base}}/api/expenses
Host: {{tenant1}}

> {% client.global.set("tenant1ExpenseId", response.body[0].id); %}

### 2. tenant2 sees only its own expenses
GET {{base}}/api/expenses
Host: {{tenant2}}

### 3. Totals are per company (tenant1)
GET {{base}}/api/expenses/total
Host: {{tenant1}}

### 3. Totals are per company (tenant2)
GET {{base}}/api/expenses/total
Host: {{tenant2}}

### 4. tenant1 adds an expense. No tenant in the body, Hibernate stamps it.
POST {{base}}/api/expenses
Host: {{tenant1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Printer",
  "amount": 400,
  "spentOn": "2026-09-21"
}

### 4. tenant2 still sees only its own rows
GET {{base}}/api/expenses
Host: {{tenant2}}

### 5. tenant1 opens its own expense by id -> 200
GET {{base}}/api/expenses/{{tenant1ExpenseId}}
Host: {{tenant1}}

### 5. tenant2 opens tenant1's expense by id -> 404
GET {{base}}/api/expenses/{{tenant1ExpenseId}}
Host: {{tenant2}}

### 6. Raw SQL with no WHERE clause, Postgres RLS still filters (tenant1)
GET {{base}}/api/debug/leak-test
Host: {{tenant1}}

### 6. Same raw SQL as tenant2
GET {{base}}/api/debug/leak-test
Host: {{tenant2}}

### 7. No tenant subdomain -> 404 before any business code runs
GET {{base}}/api/expenses
Host: localhost

### 7. Unknown tenant -> 404
GET {{base}}/api/expenses
Host: nobody.localhost

### Health check (no tenant needed, outside /api)
GET {{base}}/actuator/health
